**Definition 26.2 (an actual path descriptor).** For $p\in\mathcal P_D$
of length $n$, write $p_j$ for its length-$j$ prefix. Define
$\partial_p(t)=B$ when $p$ itself is initially branch. Otherwise let
$\partial_p(t)=(j,e)$ at its first original leaf, where $1\le j\le n$,
$e\in\{0,1\}$, and $\ell_0=\alpha,\ell_1=\beta$ is its label at
$p_j$. This is a mathematical function of the actual source, rather
than a supplied descriptor port. The original root is branch, so index
zero is excluded. An initially absent endpoint has one such earlier
leaf; it introduces no additional descriptor.

For mathematical witnesses only, define

$$
C_\varepsilon[u]=u,\qquad
C_{La}[u]=\langle C_a[u],\alpha\rangle,\qquad
C_{Ra}[u]=\langle\alpha,C_a[u]\rangle.
\tag{GDB.105}
$$

